[
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a function that will build a term from two terms plus an infix operator represented as a string:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"+\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"-\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"*\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"unknown op\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Let's try it:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"+\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints 7</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is it possible to write the function in a more general way, inserting the string as an infix operator?  I tried this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However it won't type check:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Application</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">argument</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span>\n<span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`term</span>\n<span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">application</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616057392,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786531108
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>TSyntax</code> is just lies on top of <code>Syntax</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616057826,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786531255
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This parses as an application though, rather than the actual notation</p>",
        "id": 616058071,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786531335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does this help?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">mkNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkSimple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"term_{op}_\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"+\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: 7 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616060197,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786532028
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Snir: unfortunately your first suggestion does not produce a usable term:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo2\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"+\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>prints</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">3</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616060274,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786532060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, its point was to answer your second issue not the first</p>",
        "id": 616060578,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786532162
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Your second suggestion works fine.  It looks like we can't produce the term with a quotation, but need to drop down to a lower-level syntax constructor.  This is the magic I was looking for.  Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 616061483,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786532460
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My quotation-fu isn't strong enough; there might be a way</p>\n<p>You could also actually parse the string (either <code>m!\"_ {op} _\"</code>, or pretty-print <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> and parse the whole thing) instead of hardcoding <code>\"term_{op}_\"</code></p>",
        "id": 616062573,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786532839
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, now let's consider the inverse problem: parsing an infix operator.  Consider this function:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parse_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"+\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"-\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"*\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"unknown op\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To test it, we can write a macro that deconstructs an expression, then puts it back together using <code>mk_expr2</code> which we wrote above.  It works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parse_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mk_expr2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints 5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is it possible to write parse_expr in a more general way, capturing any infix operator into a string?</p>",
        "id": 616064973,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786533630
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parse_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"unknown op\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616065846,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786533935
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It mostly depends on how strict you want to be, this function accepts a lot of things that aren't infix operators</p>",
        "id": 616065988,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786533982
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting.  Your suggestion works - that's great.  Instead of .mk, you could just use angle brackets:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨.</span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It's true that this might capture syntax that isn't an infix operator.  However, I think it should be possible to add additional checks, e.g. testing for a string that matches particular operators of interest.  So this should be good enough for me.  Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 616067528,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786534502
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>why do you want to do this? this seems like a very strange thing to do</p>",
        "id": 616067665,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786534543
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm experimenting with writing code that can translate natural-language math (with a restricted syntax/grammar) into Lean.  Yes, this is outside the scope of most typical uses of Lean macros.  :)</p>",
        "id": 616068298,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1786534786
    }
]